---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much do Xenett and Financial Cents Month-End Close cost?', 'Xenett: AI Financials Review $7.50/client/mo, Workflow $10/client/mo, unlimited users, Enterprise custom. Financial Cents Month-End Close: $5/client/mo billed annually, on top of a plan (Solo $19/mo, Team $49/user/mo, Scale $69/user/mo annual).'],
  ['Which works with Xero?', 'Xenett works with QuickBooks Online and Xero. Financial Cents Month-End Close works with QuickBooks Online, and corrections sync back to QBO.'],
  ['Which is cheaper for a 3-person firm with 20 clients?', 'Starting from nothing, Financial Cents Team for 3 users ($147) plus Month-End Close ($100) is $247/mo, vs Xenett Workflow at $200/mo with unlimited users. A solo firm pays $119/mo on Financial Cents Solo plus Month-End Close, below Xenett Workflow.'],
  ['What does each review check?', 'Xenett checks duplicate entries and vendors, GL inconsistencies, AR/AP issues, undeposited funds, uncategorized entries and missing name/class/location, plus custom review points. Financial Cents Month-End Close covers transaction review, uncategorized transactions, account reconciliation, 1099 and W-9 prep, shared transactions, and new vendors and accounts.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Xenett vs Financial Cents Month-End Close for bookkeeping firms — compared"
  description="Xenett AI Financials Review vs the Financial Cents Month-End Close add-on: per-client pricing, QBO and Xero support, what each review catches, and 20-client cost math. Prices verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Xenett vs Financial Cents Month-End Close</h1>
  <p>Both help a bookkeeping firm review client books before close. Xenett scans each client's P&amp;L and Balance Sheet for issues and works with QuickBooks Online and Xero. Financial Cents Month-End Close (MEC) is a $5/client add-on to its practice management plans that reviews and fixes client books and syncs corrections back to QuickBooks Online.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/xenett`}>Xenett</a></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/financial-cents`}>Financial Cents MEC</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Firms with QBO and Xero clients that want an automated review of every file, with unlimited users</td><td>Firms already on (or moving to) Financial Cents with QBO clients, where uncategorized transactions are the bottleneck</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</td><td>AI Financials Review $7.50/client/mo; Workflow $10/client/mo (adds projects, tasks, time tracking); add-ons Accruals + AI $15/client/mo and Inter-company Rec $10/client/mo; Enterprise custom. Unlimited users.</td><td>MEC add-on $5/client/mo, billed annually, on top of a plan: Solo $19/mo, Team $49/user/mo, Scale $69/user/mo (annual). 12-month agreement.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ledgers</td><td>QuickBooks Online and Xero</td><td>QuickBooks Online (corrections sync back to QBO)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>What the review covers</td><td>Default review points: duplicate entries and vendors, GL inconsistencies, AR/AP issues, undeposited funds, uncategorized entries, entries missing name/class/location; custom review points</td><td>Transaction review, uncategorized transactions, account reconciliation, 1099 and W-9 prep, shared transactions, new vendors and accounts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Client questions</td><td>White-labeled client portal for transaction questions with email/text reminders</td><td>Client tasks and requests with automatic follow-ups (auto follow-ups on Scale)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Where you work</td><td>Xenett app plus a browser extension inside QBO and Xero</td><td>Inside Financial Cents, next to your workflows and client portal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Trial</td><td>14-day free trial</td><td>14-day free trial on plans; MEC is added after a demo</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost for a 3-person firm with 20 clients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Already on Financial Cents: MEC adds $100/mo (20 × $5). Xenett AI Financials Review on top would be $150/mo (20 × $7.50).</li>
    <li>Starting from nothing: Financial Cents Team for 3 users ($147) plus MEC ($100) is $247/mo. Xenett Workflow is $200/mo (20 × $10) with unlimited users, but its practice management is lighter (no billing or proposals listed).</li>
    <li>Solo firm: Financial Cents Solo ($19) plus MEC ($100) is $119/mo, below Xenett Workflow at $200/mo.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>All figures are list prices, annual billing where offered, before discounts or promotions.</p>

  <h2>When to choose Xenett</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You have Xero clients, or a mix of QBO and Xero.</li>
    <li>You want a broad automated check of every file (duplicates, GL coding, AR/AP, missing class/location), not just uncategorized lines.</li>
    <li>Your team is growing and per-user pricing would hurt; Xenett charges per client.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Financial Cents MEC</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You already run the firm on Financial Cents, so the review is $5/client and sits next to your workflows.</li>
    <li>All your clients are on QuickBooks Online.</li>
    <li>Your main close problem is uncategorized transactions and client follow-up, plus 1099/W-9 prep.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: xenett.com/pricing and financial-cents.com/pricing, checked 2026-10-18. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/category/month-end-close`}>All month-end close tools</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/karbon-vs-financial-cents`}>Karbon vs Financial Cents</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/uncategorized-transactions-tools`}>Uncategorized transactions tools</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/bank-reconciliation-tools`}>Bank reconciliation tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
